y mother’s sons were angry with me. They made me keeper of the vineyards. I haven’t kept my own vineyard."},{"verse":7,"text":"Tell me, you whom my soul loves, where you graze your flock, where you rest them at noon; for why should I be as one who is veiled beside the flocks of your companions?"},{"verse":8,"text":"If you don’t know, most beautiful among women, follow the tracks of the sheep. Graze your young goats beside the shepherds’ tents."},{"verse":9,"text":"I have compared you, my love, to a steed in Pharaoh’s chariots."},{"verse":10,"text":"Your cheeks are beautiful with earrings, your neck with strings of jewels."},{"verse":11,"text":"We will make you earrings of gold, with studs of silver."},{"verse":12,"text":"While the king sat at his table, my perfume spread its fragrance."},{"verse":13,"text":"My beloved is to me a sachet of myrrh, that lies between my breasts."},{"verse":14,"text":"My beloved is to me a cluster of henna blossoms from the vineyards of En Gedi."},{"verse":15,"text":"Behold, you are beautiful, my love. Behold, you are beautiful. Your eyes are like doves."},{"verse":16,"text":"Behold, you are beautiful, my beloved, yes, pleasant; and our couch is verdant."},{"verse":17,"text":"The beams of our house are cedars. Our rafters are firs."}],"hasArtwork":false,"availableLangs":[]}]